commit 0dba92688a590bccdef1fd0116d34a26c7190601
Author: agent-b <agent-b@example.invalid>
Date:   Sun Sep 27 22:20:03 2026 +0300

    Add a waitlist for full events
    
    People can join the waitlist of an event that is full:
    POST /api/events/{id}/waitlist {"attendee": name}
      201 added (with 1-based position), 200 already on it (same position),
      409 event still has places, 404 no such event, 422 no name.
    Events now report a "waitlisted" count. On the page, a full event shows
    "Join waitlist" instead of a disabled Reserve button.
    
    Schema change (additive only): new `waitlist` table with
    UNIQUE(event_id, attendee). Existing tables are untouched; existing
    databases pick the table up via CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS on startup.
    
    The full-check and insert run in one BEGIN IMMEDIATE transaction, so
    simultaneous joiners get distinct positions. Waitlist entries never count
    towards capacity, so the promise reservations <= capacity is unaffected.
    
    Not included: promotion off the waitlist. The app has no cancellation
    or capacity change yet, so a place never frees up.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

